1
00:00:02,460 --> 00:00:05,100
=The Truth (Season 4)=
(New bonus scenes)

2
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:07,420
(Snack time gets lively)

3
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:10,040
He's tall. Give him two.

4
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:11,610
(Tall guy special)
Thanks.

5
00:00:11,640 --> 00:00:12,510
He's tall too.

6
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:13,190
Here, this one's for you.

7
00:00:13,340 --> 00:00:14,110
(Tall guys get double)
No.

8
00:00:14,110 --> 00:00:14,720
Keep it for yourself.

9
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:16,430
This one's matcha.

10
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:17,060
Yep.

11
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:19,470
What's matcha, everyone?

12
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:22,550
(Knowledge +1)
It's tea that's been ground into powder.

13
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:24,180
(So that's what it is)

14
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:26,910
Someone's been into yours.

15
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:29,750
Really?

16
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,260
Where's your matcha?

17
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:32,640
Where's his matcha?

18
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:33,970
This is Tieguanyin.

19
00:00:33,970 --> 00:00:34,830
Not matcha.

20
00:00:34,830 --> 00:00:37,960
(The truth is finally revealed)
So Tieguanyin isn't tea?

21
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:39,130
It is tea.

22
00:00:39,350 --> 00:00:40,630
Yeah, they're all tea.

23
00:00:40,870 --> 00:00:41,820
It's just tea powder.

24
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:44,350
There's a piece
of seaweed underneath this.

25
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:45,960
(What does that mean?)
What's that for?

26
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:46,600
For extra flavor.

27
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,190
(An experienced foodie)
It brings out the aroma.

28
00:00:48,470 --> 00:00:50,110
What do you guys think?

29
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:51,710
(One bite and you're speechless)
It's good.

30
00:00:52,120 --> 00:00:53,310
(Added to the must-try list)
Not bad.

31
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:54,930
This is dried pineapple.

32
00:00:54,930 --> 00:00:57,290
(Save the best for last)
Got it. I'll save it for New Year's.

33
00:00:57,320 --> 00:00:59,140
(This is getting way off track)
Save it for your next life.

34
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:00,640
(What do you mean?)
Save it for the next life?

35
00:01:00,670 --> 00:01:01,940
(Exactly)
For you.

36
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,000
For me?

37
00:01:04,370 --> 00:01:05,390
They're coming after you.

38
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:06,870
(Twelve out of ten suspicious)
Do you guys know something?

39
00:01:07,160 --> 00:01:09,430
Let's stop cursing Chancellor Tui
all the time,

40
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:10,190
okay?

41
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,990
We wish you happiness
and good health in your next life.

42
00:01:13,060 --> 00:01:14,180
(Why does that blessing sound so weird?)

43
00:01:14,560 --> 00:01:15,830
Come on, let's toast
with some dried pineapple.

44
00:01:15,840 --> 00:01:16,940
Cheers.

45
00:01:16,940 --> 00:01:17,450
(Full ceremony mode)
Cheers.

46
00:01:17,450 --> 00:01:18,010
Come on.

47
00:01:18,010 --> 00:01:19,130
Okay.

48
00:01:24,240 --> 00:01:26,000
(Can't tell who's in charge)
What do you mean?

49
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:26,960
(A friendly reminder)
Chancellor Tui's chopsticks.

50
00:01:26,970 --> 00:01:27,750
Chancellor Tui's chopsticks.

51
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:30,110
(Enjoying the chaos)
Your people don't respect you.

52
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:32,020
(Top-notch service)

53
00:01:32,480 --> 00:01:32,950
What does that mean?

54
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:36,390
(Five-star service)
He brushed all the crumbs off for us.

55
00:01:36,400 --> 00:01:38,950
He must've worked in customer service
since he was a kid.

56
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:40,220
(That's some serious skill)
He's got great service instincts.

57
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,540
Why not change the tablecloth?

58
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:43,910
Just flip the table over.

59
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,670
And there's a performance too?

60
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:47,390
What does that mean?

61
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:53,430
That part can be pulled.

62
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:54,220
Pull it apart.

63
00:01:54,220 --> 00:01:55,280
Pull it. Yeah.

64
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:56,360
No.

65
00:01:57,440 --> 00:01:58,550
Just look at him.

66
00:01:58,560 --> 00:01:59,750
(The sheltered noble)
He knows nothing about everyday life.

67
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:01,230
Yeah, he's never done any real work.

68
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:02,590
You guys are so clueless.

69
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:04,940
Go help the man already.

70
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:06,780
(At least someone noticed)

71
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,030
He's so weird.

72
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:11,160
Do you want to pull this up?

73
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:11,790
No, leave it.

74
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:12,340
Okay, leave it.

75
00:02:12,340 --> 00:02:12,950
Leave it.

76
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:14,470
No more pulling.

77
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:15,900
It's Prague now.

78
00:02:16,480 --> 00:02:20,110
Now that we've eaten

79
00:02:20,120 --> 00:02:21,350
our fill,

80
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:22,990
(Time to get down to business)
let's talk business.

81
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:26,700
(Tui City young heroes' chit-chat time)

82
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:28,900
I didn't notice yesterday

83
00:02:28,900 --> 00:02:30,560
that there was something on this knife.

84
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:32,320
I spent so long messing with it.

85
00:02:32,320 --> 00:02:33,280
Man...

86
00:02:33,280 --> 00:02:34,270
What a shame.

87
00:02:34,270 --> 00:02:35,500
I'm so pissed.

88
00:02:35,500 --> 00:02:36,790
And I just happened

89
00:02:36,790 --> 00:02:38,700
to take the two weapons you use most.

90
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:39,370
Exactly.

91
00:02:39,370 --> 00:02:41,110
It was in the sword slot.

92
00:02:41,110 --> 00:02:42,380
Oh, in the sword slot.

93
00:02:42,380 --> 00:02:42,880
Yeah.

94
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:43,470
Look.

95
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:45,470
So it's like this?

96
00:02:45,630 --> 00:02:47,890
That's clearly from being struck.

97
00:02:47,890 --> 00:02:48,460
Yeah.

98
00:02:48,460 --> 00:02:49,010
It's just

99
00:02:49,010 --> 00:02:50,730
a mark left behind.

100
00:02:50,730 --> 00:02:52,150
But it's pretty silver too.

101
00:02:52,350 --> 00:02:54,030
Once I figured out the murder method,

102
00:02:54,030 --> 00:02:55,210
I started wondering

103
00:02:55,210 --> 00:02:56,800
if we should look for the murder weapon.

104
00:02:57,360 --> 00:02:58,590
If we find the murder weapon,

105
00:02:58,590 --> 00:03:00,250
it could point straight to you.

106
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:02,910
Not a good day to make a move.

107
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:04,950
What's with your outfit today?

108
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:07,150
Doesn't he look like Uncle Wuzhu

109
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,670
from "Joy of Life"?

110
00:03:10,420 --> 00:03:11,000
Right?

111
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:11,390
Yeah.

112
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,140
How did your outfit give you pecs?

113
00:03:14,140 --> 00:03:14,740
(Helping fix his clothes)

114
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:16,000
It's too loose.

115
00:03:16,480 --> 00:03:17,870
Why did you pull my pants out?

116
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:19,420
(Starting to investigate the outfit)
It's probably too loose.

117
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:20,080
What's going on?

118
00:03:20,080 --> 00:03:21,140
Why doesn't it fit right?

119
00:03:21,160 --> 00:03:22,540
Our belts are the same.

120
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:23,580
Really?

121
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:24,950
Is it this one?

122
00:03:24,960 --> 00:03:27,390
Why does it look so bulky?

123
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:29,970
It's because this part
isn't pulled flat.

124
00:03:30,260 --> 00:03:33,230
It looks like you're hiding
a lot of things here.

125
00:03:33,730 --> 00:03:35,120
A lot of secrets.

126
00:03:35,120 --> 00:03:35,700
(Jin's humor)

127
00:03:36,220 --> 00:03:37,460
(Serious recap)

128
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,290
Don't look, little killer.

129
00:03:39,290 --> 00:03:39,600
Yeah.

130
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:41,960
She's been studying the script all day.

131
00:03:42,170 --> 00:03:43,930
(He will explain it to you)
The killer's script is complicated.

132
00:03:43,930 --> 00:03:45,140
She has to pick and choose.

133
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:47,360
(Evil whispering)
Oh, stop talking.

134
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:48,620
(Just see if I stab you)

135
00:03:49,450 --> 00:03:50,320
Let's go.

136
00:03:50,320 --> 00:03:51,180
I'm your big brother.

137
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,310
I'm on a killing spree.

138
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:55,750
You've completely lost it.

139
00:03:55,760 --> 00:04:00,550
Let's check out Chivalry Manor now.

140
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,410
Once we're inside,

141
00:04:01,410 --> 00:04:02,230
you go first.

142
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,070
I've got my guards.

143
00:04:05,060 --> 00:04:07,340
(Detective team looking out
for each other while scared)

144
00:04:07,480 --> 00:04:08,430
(Night vision mode)
Come on, guys.

145
00:04:08,440 --> 00:04:09,870
(Eyes tightly shut)
What are we supposed to do?

146
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:10,630
(Horror elements for fictional use)
The candle's lit.

147
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:11,180
Wait.

148
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:12,230
(Jin is scared)
What's going on?

149
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,070
It's okay.

150
00:04:13,080 --> 00:04:14,910
(Ning's guess)
The ghost soldiers should come out.

151
00:04:14,920 --> 00:04:15,590
But we...

152
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:18,070
We might be the ghost soldiers.

153
00:04:18,080 --> 00:04:19,270
No way.

154
00:04:19,280 --> 00:04:21,310
We must've turned
into ghost soldiers already.

155
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:22,710
There's only one living person among us.

156
00:04:23,220 --> 00:04:26,180
(What?)

157
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:27,020
(Successfully made the others laugh)

158
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:27,950
What are you scared of?

159
00:04:27,960 --> 00:04:28,990
It's lit up inside.

160
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:29,630
Look inside.

161
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:30,750
(The atmosphere is intense)
Red light.

162
00:04:30,760 --> 00:04:31,270
The back.

163
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:32,130
Behind you.

164
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:33,870
This side.

165
00:04:33,880 --> 00:04:35,870
(Imaginations are running wild)
Are two people supposed to lie in here?

166
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:37,670
(Ke steps up)
Don't rush. Let me take a look, okay?

167
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:38,910
Let's go together.

168
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,020
Wait.

169
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:41,130
Watch out for the steps.

170
00:04:41,130 --> 00:04:42,960
(So scared she's stuttering)
Jin, I really...

171
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:45,200
(Ning is right beside you)
Come on, go find Ning.

172
00:04:45,200 --> 00:04:47,250
I don't know where he is.

173
00:04:47,250 --> 00:04:48,300
(Ning comes to get you)
Come back.

174
00:04:48,300 --> 00:04:48,860
Where is everyone?

175
00:04:48,860 --> 00:04:50,260
(Something big is coming. Memorial)

176
00:04:50,300 --> 00:04:50,700
(Holding tight)

177
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:53,090
It's okay.

178
00:04:53,090 --> 00:04:54,160
The ghost soldiers are here.

179
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,120
Stand up.

180
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:56,110
(Caring)
Don't step on her.

181
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,100
You grab her.

182
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:57,780
Grab her.

183
00:04:57,780 --> 00:04:58,770
Okay.

184
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:00,030
I'll give you my arm.

185
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:01,710
(The best Ning)
Hold on.

186
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:02,450
He...

187
00:05:02,450 --> 00:05:03,220
He is...

188
00:05:03,660 --> 00:05:04,420
(Closing in step by step)

189
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:05,340
Okay.

190
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:06,260
Hold on.

191
00:05:07,360 --> 00:05:09,630
(Ke comes to protect you)
It's okay.

192
00:05:09,640 --> 00:05:12,830
(Really scared)
Jin, I was so scared I almost cried.

193
00:05:12,840 --> 00:05:14,920
(Trying to convince them)
We're all ghost soldiers.

194
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:16,020
We're on the same side.

195
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:19,130
Stop.

196
00:05:19,130 --> 00:05:19,740
What?

197
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:20,580
Careful.

198
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:21,020
(Safe for now)
It's okay.

199
00:05:21,020 --> 00:05:21,380
(Ding has grown braver)

200
00:05:21,380 --> 00:05:22,880
Where is he driving us?

201
00:05:22,880 --> 00:05:24,070
He's trying to get us inside.

202
00:05:24,080 --> 00:05:25,110
Wait, let me check.

203
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:25,750
See if it opens.

204
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:27,230
Let's open the door.

205
00:05:27,230 --> 00:05:28,280
We can go in.

206
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:29,040
Okay, okay, let's go in.

207
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:32,260
(Winning over the soldiers with love)

208
00:05:32,280 --> 00:05:35,910
(Ning scares everyone)
The alchemy room has test zombies.

209
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:37,620
(A little scary)

210
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:39,670
They're all super soldiers.

211
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:42,910
Don't you have a way to deal
with super soldiers?

212
00:05:43,600 --> 00:05:44,990
(Generating power with love)
Give them a deep kiss.

213
00:05:45,380 --> 00:05:46,020
(A little too much like a romance)

214
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:48,550
Exactly. We cure them with love.

215
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:50,020
Just kiss them and they'll be cured.

216
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:50,940
(Does it work)

217
00:05:51,140 --> 00:05:52,060
(like this?)

218
00:05:52,080 --> 00:05:53,710
(Kiss to clear the way)
When the time comes, just kiss them.

219
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:57,370
(Kissing the situation under control)
So that's what you meant.

220
00:05:57,370 --> 00:05:58,730
Kiss to clear the way.

221
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:01,750
What was the Crown Prince writing?

222
00:06:01,760 --> 00:06:03,880
(Focused)
I was writing this character.

223
00:06:04,240 --> 00:06:05,840
Go out this way.

224
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:06,590
Go out.

225
00:06:06,590 --> 00:06:07,870
This way, right?

226
00:06:07,870 --> 00:06:08,440
I can't see anything.

227
00:06:08,480 --> 00:06:09,750
Go out and cross the bridge.

228
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:11,150
Go out and turn right.

229
00:06:11,150 --> 00:06:13,060
Then go up and turn left.

230
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:13,300
Right.

231
00:06:13,320 --> 00:06:14,910
Turn left, go up, then turn left again.

232
00:06:15,240 --> 00:06:15,790
Let's go.

233
00:06:15,790 --> 00:06:16,380
Go.

234
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:18,700
(Detective team makes good use
of Massage Card)

235
00:06:19,560 --> 00:06:20,830
You have so many cards.

236
00:06:20,840 --> 00:06:21,910
(Ding's: Item, Hint, Dancing, Massage+2)
Dancing, Massage Card.

237
00:06:21,920 --> 00:06:22,630
They're all useless.

238
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:23,790
(Ning takes a look)
Take a look yourself.

239
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:24,390
What cards are those?

240
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:25,510
Two Massage Cards.

241
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,270
(Thinking outside the box)
We can use these on the ghost soldiers.

242
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:27,630
Right.

243
00:06:27,640 --> 00:06:27,990
Have the Princess and Crown Prince

244
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:30,390
(Unique service)
take turns massaging you later.

245
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,100
Have the ghost soldiers massage you.

246
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:33,530
Yeah, let them massage you.

247
00:06:33,530 --> 00:06:34,250
It's so exhausted.

248
00:06:34,250 --> 00:06:35,740
Why not use a Massage Card?

249
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:36,780
Do it yourself?

250
00:06:37,400 --> 00:06:38,730
(Not enough)
It only lasts three minutes.

251
00:06:38,730 --> 00:06:40,180
(Ke has an idea)
I think next time you should like...

252
00:06:40,180 --> 00:06:40,580
I mean,

253
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:42,430
when you meet some really powerful NPC,

254
00:06:42,440 --> 00:06:43,830
like someone who's truly supreme,

255
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:45,480
some kind of revered master,

256
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:46,550
just tell them to give you a massage.

257
00:06:46,560 --> 00:06:47,350
Then they actually do it.

258
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:47,990
But what if

259
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:48,870
they lose control and get angry

260
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:49,670
afterward?

261
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:51,390
(Pleasure first)
That's okay. Let's enjoy it first.

262
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:53,510
Say you run into a deadly challenge.

263
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:54,670
(Just enjoy it)
Enjoy it first before dealing with it.

264
00:06:54,680 --> 00:06:57,190
You should've had
the ghost soldiers massage you.

265
00:06:57,760 --> 00:07:00,390
(Hardcore massage booked)
Three minutes of that is like thirty.

266
00:07:02,580 --> 00:07:03,520
=The Truth (Season 4)=

267
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,540
(SVIP updates Wed & Thu at 12PM.)

268
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:05,660
(VIP updates next day at 12PM,
one week early.)
